,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nCurrent `master`\n\n### System information\n\nLinux Mint 20.3 - `master` - `gcc (Ubuntu 9.4.0-1ubuntu1~20.04.2) 9.4.0` \n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen compiling from source using GCC, this error shows up in the terminal:\n```\ng++: error: unrecognized command line option '-Wenum-conversion'; did you mean '-Wno-conversion'?\n```\nCompiling with Clang works as expected. \n\nThis seems to be coming from a recent change in the `SConstruct`. Line 893 sets that flag:\n```\n    common_warnings = [\"-Wenum-conversion\"]\n```\nAccording to docs I found for warnings with GCC, the `-Wenum-conversion` flag seems to only work in C, not C++\nhttps://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-12.1.0/gcc/Warning-Options.html#Warning-Options\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Pull Godot source from `master`\n2. Build with these flags: `scons platform=linux`\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"Us